course: dictionary
lesson: 10481
title: Turbine: machines that spin to make power
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A turbine is a machine with blades. Moving wind, water, steam or gas turns the blades, and the turning is used to make electricity or power.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Offshore wind farms are rows of turbines standing in the sea» tells you that turbines stand up tall, and the wind and the electricity are clues too. A wind farm is a group of wind turbines standing together.
explain: Turbines is the plural, so one turbine becomes many turbines. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: «Tidal power stations use the tides to spin underwater turbines.» Does a machine with spinning blades fit? Yes, so your meaning works.
fact: A turbine is a machine with blades that are turned by moving wind, water, steam or gas.
fact: A wind turbine is a tall tower with big blades that the wind spins to make electricity.
fact: A wind farm is a group of wind turbines standing together.
fact: Power stations burn fuel to boil water into steam, and the steam spins turbines.
fact: «Turbines» means more than one turbine.
exercise: «Offshore wind farms are rows of turbines standing in the sea.» What is a turbine? | A type of fish that lives in the sea | A tall ship with sails | A cable that carries electricity | *A machine with blades turned by moving wind, water, steam or gas
exercise: «Coal, oil and gas power stations burn fuel to boil water into steam that spins turbines.» What spins the turbines? | The Moon | Rain | *Steam | Sunlight
exercise: «A tidal power station uses the tides flowing in and out to spin underwater turbines.» Find and copy the word that means under the water. | tidal | station | power | *underwater
test: «Wind turbines make electricity from the wind.» What does a wind turbine do with the wind? | Makes the wind stop | Turns the wind into sand | *Spins its blades to make electricity | Sends the wind under the sea
test: «Engineers have copied the bumps on humpback whale flippers for fan and turbine blades.» What does this tell you? | Whales are machines | *Engineers can learn ideas from nature | Fans are made of whales | Turbines live in the sea
exam: What is a wind farm? | A machine that cooks food | A tall ship on the sea | *A group of wind turbines standing together
